# ---- Build output -------------------------------------------------------
/bin/
/dist/
/walkie
/walkie-coordinator
*.exe

# ---- Go -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
/vendor/

# ---- Runtime state and secrets ------------------------------------------
# adr:004-security-model has each device generate an X25519 identity keypair
# on first run and store it on disk. Committing one would be a real incident,
# not a style problem. The coordinator's queue and the client's history are
# SQLite files holding message content.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.key
*.pem
*.sock
/.walkie/

# ---- Local environment --------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Editors and OS -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- Agent local settings -----------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# =========================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored — do not "tidy" these into the list above.
#
#   exchange/           The EKA knowledge snapshot, generated by `eka sync`
#                       and committed on purpose so the engineering knowledge
#                       travels with the repository. Regenerate with
#                       `eka sync`, never by hand.
#
#   internal/genproto/  Generated protobuf code, committed on purpose so that
#                       `go build` works with no codegen toolchain installed
#                       — which matters for ARM devices and new contributors.
#                       CI enforces that it stays in sync with proto/.
# =========================================================================
/.eka/
